  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best (config_039, acc=0.7250) uses multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted. All component choices are well-supported by evidence: scvi_n200 >> pca_n2000 >> scgpt, imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, weighted > concat, multiprofile >> singleprofile. The only untested variation on this optimal stack is aggregation: avgpool vs. transformer. In RNA-only, these were nearly identical (0.6530 vs 0.6501), but in the multimodal setting with a strong ViT encoder, the interaction between aggregation and cross-modal fusion may differ. Config_037 (avgpool + weighted + imagenet_vit_l + scvi_n200 + multiprofile) isolates exactly this one change. As the final experiment, this is the highest-probability exploitation step: it keeps every other setting at its empirically validated optimum and tests the single remaining unexplored degree of freedom, giving the best chance of marginally exceeding 0.7250."
}

